
# [ ] 🧱 Phase 1 — Core Stability (must be done first)

### ✔ Project structure & execution

* [x] Add `archiverr/__main__.py`
* [ ] Fix CLI entry via Typer (`app()` working)
* [ ] Add `pyproject.toml` script entry (`archiverr = ...`)
* [ ] Ensure `pip install -e .` works cleanly

---

### ✔ Data model correctness

* [ ] Finalise `Track` dataclass (no ordering bugs)
* [ ] Finalise `Library` + `Playlist` models
* [ ] Ensure all optional fields are consistent (`None` vs defaults)
* [ ] Add `raw_apple_data` preservation everywhere

---

### ✔ Apple Music ingestion (core input)

* [ ] Fully parse `Library.xml` (tracks + playlists)
* [ ] Parse ALL useful fields:

  * [ ] Track metadata
  * [ ] Play counts
  * [ ] Dates (added, modified, played)
  * [ ] Protected / Apple Music flags
  * [ ] File location decoding
* [ ] Validate parsing on large library (10k+ tracks)

---

# 🗃 Phase 2 — Local Database (turn it into a system)

### ✔ SQLite warehouse

* [ ] Implement `init_db()`
* [ ] Create schema migration system (even simple versioned SQL files)
* [ ] Add:

  * [ ] `insert_track`
  * [ ] `update_track`
  * [ ] `get_track_by_id`
  * [ ] `bulk_insert_tracks`

---

### ✔ Canonical ID system (critical)

* [ ] Implement deterministic `canonical_id`
* [ ] Ensure it uses:

  * artist
  * title
  * album
  * duration
* [ ] Store canonical ID in DB immediately on ingest

---

### ✔ Ingestion pipeline v1

* [ ] `archiverr ingest <Library.xml>`
* [ ] Parse → normalize → assign IDs → store in DB
* [ ] Output stats:

  * total tracks
  * protected tracks
  * missing metadata

---

# 🔍 Phase 3 — Metadata Resolution Layer

### ✔ Spotify resolver

* [ ] Search by artist + track
* [ ] Add fuzzy matching (rapidfuzz)
* [ ] Store:

  * Spotify ID
  * ISRC (if available)
  * confidence score

---

### ✔ MusicBrainz resolver

* [ ] Query recordings
* [ ] Match by:

  * ISRC (priority)
  * duration
  * artist/title fallback
* [ ] Cache results locally (VERY important)

---

### ✔ YouTube resolver

* [ ] yt-dlp search integration
* [ ] Select best “official audio” candidate
* [ ] Store YouTube URL + ID

---

### ✔ Metadata merge engine

* [ ] Combine all sources into unified record
* [ ] Resolve conflicts using confidence scoring
* [ ] Store final “resolved metadata” in DB

---

# ⬇️ Phase 4 — Download System (turn it into an archiver)

### ✔ yt-dlp downloader

* [ ] Download highest quality audio
* [ ] Output format:

  ```
  /archive/{artist}/{album}/{track}.ext
  ```

---

### ✔ Download scheduler

* [ ] Queue system (async or threaded)
* [ ] Retry logic
* [ ] Resume support

---

### ✔ File verification

* [ ] Hashing (SHA256 or BLAKE3)
* [ ] Detect duplicates
* [ ] Skip already downloaded files

---

### ✔ Source ranking system

* [ ] Prefer:

  * official uploads
  * correct duration match
  * highest bitrate
* [ ] Reject:

  * lyric videos
  * sped-up/slowed versions
  * reuploads

---

